WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:06.240
Before we start today’s video, we need to ask you&nbsp;
a question: Are you alone in the room? Seriously,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:12.640
are you alone? You may think that the room around&nbsp;
you is empty, but how can you really know that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:18.320
right? Think of the technology out there being&nbsp;
developed by groups like DARPA, the CIA, or even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:24.160
the SCP Foundation - Secret agents in cloaking&nbsp;
suits could be standing around you right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:28.800
watching your every move, without you even&nbsp;
knowing. You could tell someone about this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:34.240
but if you did, they’d think you’re crazy,&nbsp;
and nobody believes crazy people, do they?

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:39.680
Sometimes people’s whole worlds just collapse.&nbsp;
One day they’re living happy, successful lives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:44.560
with families and friends who love and care&nbsp;
about them. Then the next day, they’re truly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:49.280
convinced that the US government is tapping&nbsp;
not only their phone calls and their emails,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:55.440
but their thoughts. Perhaps even putting dangerous&nbsp;
brainwaves directly into their mind. Or they start&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.440 --> 00:01:00.560
to believe that those loving family members and&nbsp;
friends seek to do them harm. Maybe they start to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:06.480
believe their food is poisoned, and stop eating,&nbsp;
causing them to waste away from malnutrition.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:11.600
Most terrifying of all, maybe they start&nbsp;
to see things that nobody else could see.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:19.040
Monsters that defy rationality and shake&nbsp;
the very soul. Terrible, terrible things…

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:23.360
These are all, sadly, relatively common&nbsp;
symptoms of someone suffering from a severe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:28.960
case of Schizophrenia - A mental illness with a&nbsp;
wide range of detrimental effects to sufferers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:33.680
first and foremost giving them an incredibly&nbsp;
complicated relationship with reality.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:38.000
There’s sadly a lot of misconceptions in the&nbsp;
media about people who suffer from illnesses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:43.360
like Schizophrenia, painting them as unstable&nbsp;
individuals who present a danger to the people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:48.400
around them. In reality, people with a condition&nbsp;
like this are three times more likely to be the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:53.840
victim of a violent crime. And they’re also more&nbsp;
likely to be the victim of something else, too...

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:58.560
Like we said earlier, sometimes&nbsp;
people’s worlds just collapse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:02.720
and in severe cases, they&nbsp;
might simply drop off the map.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:10.400
And nine times out of ten, the reason for&nbsp;
that is SCP-870: The Maybe There Monsters.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:14.800
Take the experience of Katrina Wayne.&nbsp;
She was an office temp in Tallahassee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:19.040
Florida, with an undiagnosed case of&nbsp;
mild schizophrenia. For the most part,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:24.000
she was able to operate just fine at her job,&nbsp;
getting her work done at a satisfactory level&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:29.120
while also maintaining a decent social life after&nbsp;
hours. It came as a shock to everyone when she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:34.320
began screeching horrifically in the middle of the&nbsp;
office. She backed herself up against the wall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:39.120
picking up nearby objects and throwing&nbsp;
them into the aisles at some invisible foe.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:44.240
And this isn’t a metaphor: There really&nbsp;
was an invisible foe moving towards her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:50.000
and only she could truly see it. Seeing the huge,&nbsp;
scaly body of a mature alligator from the Florida&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:54.880
Everglades moving towards you would be scary&nbsp;
enough on its own, but this wasn’t any ordinary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.880 --> 00:03:01.040
alligator. Its long, reptilian head had three eyes&nbsp;
instead of two, and it moved towards her on eight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:06.720
huge, articulated spider legs. It was like&nbsp;
something straight out of a nightmare.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:09.120
Katrina was put on leave due to a stress-induced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:13.840
mental breakdown and prescribed a course of&nbsp;
antipsychotic medication by a psychiatrist.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:17.920
She disappeared from her home without&nbsp;
a trace a mere two weeks later.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:22.240
Or take the story of Daryl Simon. He was a&nbsp;
mechanic working in Michigan with a family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:27.360
history of schizophrenia, though he’d never been&nbsp;
officially diagnosed himself. He was working on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:33.200
the engine of a vintage corvette when something&nbsp;
strange happened: His garage began to fill up with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:38.160
smoke. He considered at first that perhaps it was&nbsp;
some kind of engine malfunction causing smoke to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:44.000
belch out of the old corvette’s tailpipe, but then&nbsp;
he saw something standing in the smoke - A human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:48.400
figure. Daryl suddenly felt a profound&nbsp;
sense of dread seeping into his mind.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:52.640
He grabbed a monkey wrench and began to slowly&nbsp;
approach the intruder standing in the smoke.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:55.920
It was only when he was already too close&nbsp;
that he realized that the figure wasn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.920 --> 00:04:00.800
just standing in the smoke. It was made&nbsp;
of smoke. The second he noticed this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:06.880
the figure’s eyes opened, glowing red. Its smoky&nbsp;
face opened into a wide, toothy mouth and let out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:12.160
an ear splitting shriek. Daryl suddenly found&nbsp;
himself running as the creature gave chase. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:17.120
threw his wrench at it as he ran; it breezed&nbsp;
through the creature’s semi-intangible form.

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:22.240
Daryl was found later that day, huddled in the&nbsp;
corner of his garage, muttering incoherently.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:26.480
After seeing a mental health professional and&nbsp;
sharing his story, he was given a schizophrenia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:32.400
diagnosis. He was given a mix of talk therapy and&nbsp;
medication, and seemed to be improving over time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:36.320
He would occasionally report hallucinations&nbsp;
of the man made of smoke, watching from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:41.040
corner of his eye, but it was dismissed as&nbsp;
nothing more than that: A hallucination.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:43.280
A month later, he was gone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:48.640
Never to be seen again. But he wasn’t the&nbsp;
only one to fall victim to the anomaly.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:52.800
Shirley Nicholson, a retiree whose&nbsp;
schizophrenic symptoms developed later in life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:58.320
was having a quiet evening in her home when&nbsp;
she first encountered an instance of SCP-870.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:02.880
She was watching a game show on television when&nbsp;
she heard a strange noise coming from her kitchen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:06.800
A rustling, like someone was messing&nbsp;
with the food inside her fridge.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:10.880
Of course, she’d always had a tendency to hear&nbsp;
things, which was why she wasn’t that nervous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:15.680
when she got up and walked into the kitchen.&nbsp;
That sense of confidence didn’t last long.

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:19.680
When she entered her kitchen, she saw the&nbsp;
fridge door open, with the back half of what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:24.960
looked like a giant ant emerging from it. Her&nbsp;
breath caught in her throat. That giant ant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:30.480
which seemed to be eating the food inside her&nbsp;
fridge, suddenly froze, seeming to realize that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:35.520
Shirley had entered the room. When it backed out&nbsp;
of the fridge, Shirley couldn’t help but scream.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:40.800
Instead of antennas and mandibles, the&nbsp;
giant ant had a grinning, human face.

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:45.440
As Shirley screamed, the giant ant’s human&nbsp;
face began to cackle with sadistic glee.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:50.960
Its jaw began to stretch open, impossibly&nbsp;
wide, exposing the never-ending darkness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:56.080
within. Shirley turned and ran as the creature&nbsp;
skittered towards her at a frightening speed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.080 --> 00:06:01.200
Adrenaline kicked in, and Shirley ran for her&nbsp;
life as the monster pursued her through the house.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:04.560
It was only when she ran out into the&nbsp;
street, and was seen by others in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:09.040
bizarre outburst, that the horrifying&nbsp;
ant monster seemed to disappear.

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:12.240
And several weeks after her&nbsp;
schizophrenia diagnosis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:17.760
Shirley Nicholson sadly disappeared too. Before&nbsp;
she vanished, she made a panicked 911 call,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:21.200
where she screamed down the line&nbsp;
that the monster had come back.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:26.720
No explanation has yet to be found, but there&nbsp;
are more cases to be investigated still.

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:32.480
Don Jones, who had a documented history with&nbsp;
schizophrenia, had his SCP-870 experience while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:37.760
waiting for the bus out of town late one October&nbsp;
evening. He was checking his phone at the bus stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:42.720
when he saw a figure shuffling towards him in the&nbsp;
distance. He tried to ignore it at first - Years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:47.120
of therapy had taught him to try his best&nbsp;
to ignore these strange little anomalies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:51.360
He’d been medicated for years, and while&nbsp;
occasionally he had minor episodes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:55.200
he’d lived with the condition for long&nbsp;
enough now that he’d learned how to cope.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:58.240
That’s when the strange,&nbsp;
shuffling figure got closer.

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:03.200
Don looked up, just for a moment, to see the&nbsp;
thing coming towards him out of the dark. It was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:08.160
about the size of a child, though a little shorter&nbsp;
because of how far the creature was hunched over.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:13.200
Literally, hunched, the entity had a rather&nbsp;
prominent hunchback. But this wasn’t nearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:18.560
as noticeable as the thing’s face: It had the&nbsp;
head of a particularly mangy-looking parrot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:22.240
its curved beak caked in&nbsp;
what looked like old blood.

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:26.080
This was stranger than some of the&nbsp;
hallucinations he’d suffered in the past.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:31.120
It looked more tangible, more real, even&nbsp;
after years of medication and therapy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:34.880
He felt nervous as the thing approached&nbsp;
him. On some subconscious level,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:38.720
he knew the thing intended to&nbsp;
harm him in one way or another.

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:42.960
When it opened its mouth, and sunk the&nbsp;
bladed tip of its beak into Don’s hand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:47.360
he knew that he wasn’t dealing with any&nbsp;
mundane fantasy here. He screamed and ran&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:52.320
off into the night, the monster giving chase.&nbsp;
He later reported the incident to the police,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:55.920
but his fears were written off when&nbsp;
his medical history came to light.

00:07:55.920 --> 00:08:00.480
Everyone just assumed the man was experiencing&nbsp;
another episode, and that the wound in his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:04.640
hand was self-inflicted. Of course, as&nbsp;
you’ve probably gathered by this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:08.320
poor Don Jones would disappear&nbsp;
without a trace not long after.

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:10.960
Still, the testimonies get freakier...

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:15.920
A warehouse security guard, Alex Landry, had&nbsp;
his terrifying encounter while on the job.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:20.080
He was on his nightly patrol when he heard a&nbsp;
strangely soft skittering noise coming from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:25.520
inside the warehouse. He deployed his flashlight&nbsp;
and ran inside after radioing for assistance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:29.040
He was expecting maybe an escaped&nbsp;
animal or a young hoodlum messing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:34.160
around inside. What he didn’t expect was&nbsp;
a face-to-face encounter with pure terror.

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:38.000
As his flashlight’s beam traced its&nbsp;
way up to the top of the warehouse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:43.600
he saw a monster crawling across the ceiling.&nbsp;
It was a giant, fifteen-foot-long centipede,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:48.720
but instead of having normal centipede legs,&nbsp;
it had scores of twitching, grasping human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:53.120
arms. He was found in a comatose state&nbsp;
by his partner, and spent the brief rest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:58.880
of his life in a psychiatric facility before -&nbsp;
you guessed it - disappearing without a trace.

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:02.960
And most exhilaratingly, we&nbsp;
come to the tale of Mr. Holgate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:08.560
which both ends a little more hopeful for him, but&nbsp;
paints a grim picture of what happened to everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:14.240
else. Mr. Holgate had encountered a spider-like&nbsp;
creature with a freakish number of legs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:19.120
which he soon realized only he could&nbsp;
see. During his periods of observation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:23.200
he’d seen the creature both devour a&nbsp;
ruler - as in, the measurement device,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:28.800
not a king - as well as swallow a human whole&nbsp;
after an extended period of stalking the victim,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:35.920
leaving nothing behind. Just like the SCP-870&nbsp;
instances had done to all their other victims.

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:39.760
When the monster eventually came&nbsp;
for Holgate, he was ready. It ran&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:44.800
screeching towards him on its too many legs,&nbsp;
and Holgate whipped out a gun and shot it.

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:49.040
The Foundation has prioritized the&nbsp;
capture or destruction of SCP-870.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:53.760
It’s believed to be not a single&nbsp;
instance, but an entire species,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:59.040
living out there, preying on humans and hiding&nbsp;
in the space between our perceptions. Even two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:04.320
schizophrenic people looking at the same instance&nbsp;
will report seeing completely different entities.

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:09.200
The monsters are all the more dangerous due to&nbsp;
the fact that sufferers of severe schizophrenia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:14.480
often report hallucinations of strange monsters&nbsp;
or entities, so their pleas for help are often&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:20.080
ignored by neurotypical authorities. Neurotypical&nbsp;
meaning those who don’t experience any form of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:24.320
mental illness, personality disorder,&nbsp;
or developmental condition - People&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:29.680
who could never see SCP-870 coming until&nbsp;
they’re already being swallowed whole.

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:35.280
The lead researcher on the SCP-870 case follows up&nbsp;
the file on the monsters with an ominous note that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:40.320
leaves little comfort for even those of us who&nbsp;
don’t suffer from schizophrenia. The note reads:

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:46.320
“I, personally, don't believe that the&nbsp;
schizophrenics are really seeing SCP-870 fully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:51.520
they can just see it more than us. We don't see&nbsp;
it because our brains aren't made to see it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:56.480
The schizophrenics, their brains are&nbsp;
wired up just that tiny bit differently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.480 --> 00:11:00.080
and they can see it just a tiny bit more. These&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:05.040
things have the perfect camouflage, and&nbsp;
we simply are unable to see through it.”

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:08.240
To return to what we said at the&nbsp;
very beginning of this video.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:14.000
Look around the room and answer&nbsp;
our question: Are you alone? Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:19.520
at least you know the answer to that&nbsp;
question may not be as simple as it seems...

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:22.880
Now go check out “Evil Monster&nbsp;
Created by SCP Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:30.560
SCP-2419 - The Laughing Men” and “Revenge of&nbsp;
D Class Ghosts SCP-4973 - Dead Men Walking”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:34.800
for more scary anomalous beings that’ll&nbsp;
have you looking over your shoulder!

